-- parse: prompt token word -> sequent structure (the input side of K-sl / K-tt).
--
-- input   the prompt  THM p1 , ... SEQ goal PRF  as a word over the ND alphabet (README):
--         \e THM COMMA SEQ PRF QED BAR COLON SEMI LP RP NEG AND OR IMP P Q R S F N PR ... DN. THM (... (PRF e))
-- output  seq = \s. s prems goal  (Scott list of premises, goal; formulas in the README encoding)
--
-- (Letters that never occur in a prompt -- QED | : ; N and the rules -- get an arbitrary handler.)
-- The word is a right fold, so the parser reads right to left with a stack (Scott list):
--   end: empty stack;  PRF ) , SEQ: nothing;  an atom or F: push it;  & v >: pop B, push (\A. A op B);
--   ~: pop A, push Not then A;  (: pop A, pop f, push f A;  THM: the stack is p1 ... pk goal -> (p1..pk, goal).

Y f = (\x. x x) (\x. f (x x))
I x = x
nil n c = n
cons h t n c = c h t
pair a b s = s a b
-- atom indices: Scott numerals
z0 z s = z
sc n z s = s n

Atom k t f n a o i = t k
Bot t f n a o i = f
Not x t f n a o i = n x
And x y t f n a o i = a x y
Or x y t f n a o i = o x y
Imp x y t f n a o i = i x y

push x s = cons x s
op c s = s I (\b t. cons (\a. c a b) t)
neg s = s I (\a t. cons a (cons Not t))
lp s = s I (\a t. t I (\f u. cons (f a) u))
-- last / all-but-last of a nonempty list, to a continuation
li = Y \li s k. s I (\h t. t (k nil h) (\x y. li t (\ps g. k (cons h ps) g)))

param w

main = w nil (\s. li s pair) I I I I push push push lp I neg (op And) (op Or) (op Imp)
         (push (Atom z0)) (push (Atom (sc z0))) (push (Atom (sc (sc z0)))) (push (Atom (sc (sc (sc z0))))) (push Bot)
         push push push push push push push push push push push push push push push push
